let's bring in Mike Florio from pro  football talk on NBCSN  Mike good morning how are you well just  trying to sort out this Josh Allen  situation should he have done should he  have gone through and done interviews  today well I I don't know that there's  an easy way for him to dig out of this  hole and look he's a young kid still and  he was even younger and stupider when he  did that the tweets six seven years ago  III don't I don't know at this point  what you do to undo the damage and the  problem is I think somebody must have  timed this to cause maximum mayhem right  whether it's a rival agent could be  somebody from a team that loves him and  wants to get him and you know what let's  drop this stuff out there so he slides  down and we can grab him I mean there's  all sorts of dirty things that happen  around the draft millions of dollars  riding on it futures of franchises and  it's just it's look I don't want to  defend the content it is what it is but  for it all to come up now it puts him in  the worst possible spot to try to sift  through it so you got to ask yourself am  I gonna make it better is there a chance  I'm gonna make it worse if there's any  chance I'm gonna make it worse it's  better to say nothing how do you think  teams are gonna react to this tonight I  think it just depends upon what each  individual team thinks how they assess  at what their owner thinks what the  coach thinks what's what the GM thinks  and you know yeah I am inna mum if  there's a team that calls  Josh Allen's agent says we want to get  him on the phone base you better get on  the phone with them and if they have  questions he'd better answer them or  they're just going to say forget it we  aren't we don't want this guy so even if  he doesn't say anything publicly he  better be ready to talk privately to any  team that wants to to talk to him about  this and figure out what happened of  course the broader issue is and the the  lesson to be learned apart from not  saying stupid things ever especially on  social media but when you know you're  going to be occupying a huge platform  you got to go back and clean that stuff  up and you'd think that the agent would  tell the players and if they haven't now  they need to tell them going forward you  got to go back and clean those things up  what should the Browns do tonight what  will the Browns do tonight well I don't  know what they're gonna do isn't that  fun I think teams have embraced the real  they show component of this there was a  time Dan when they would not only tell  us who they were going to take they'd  sign into a contract before the draft  what fun is that when the draft begins I  think the Browns who have been unable to  fascinate us with their performance on  the field have decided hey if we can  fascinate people with not telling them  who the number one pick in the draft is  we'll do that instead and I there's like  a twinkle in John Dorsey's eye I've  noticed when I talked to him about it  they don't want to tell anybody because  they like the fact that everyone wants  to know something about the Browns and I  this Baker Mayfield thing and there's  just thought about this kid and you know  when you think of the intangibles what  did the Browns need and if all things  are relatively equal and it really is a  crapshoot  we know it's a crapshoot John Schneider  the Seahawks GM had some great comments  earlier this week about the Aaron  Rodgers experience when he was in Green  Bay in 2005 as Rodgers is falling the  Packers don't know what to do they  haven't done the work on the guy they're  scrambling what why is he falling do we  take him do we not take him and they  take him and ends up being one of the  greatest quarterbacks of all time so if  all things are relatively equal there's  just something about Baker Mayfield that  fits with what the Browns need they need  a full reset on that franchise they need  a guy who's gonna come in there with  attitude and swagger and and I just I  feel like for me and many others it  changes instantly the perception of that  franchise if they take Baker Mayfield  and who knows but if they do I think  it's going to be one heck of a story  quarterback you don't like yes and I  have Chris Simms every day telling me  the virtues and and the benefits and the  upside of Josh Allen and and I  understand that if you play for a bad  team the product is gonna be bad but  look at his games last year he had like  four games with under a hundred passing  yards how does that happen if you're a  great quarterback I mean I guess if they  just have you hand the ball off all the  time it happens but if you're a truly  great quarterback he's gonna be a great  NFL player I feel like we're gonna see  more of that through the college  experience no matter how good or bad the  team is that you play on and that's one  of the rules of thumb I've heard over  the years you got a  dominant at the college level to have  any chance of being dominant at the NFL  level and these issues with his footwork  I know he says he's fixed them but he's  got accuracy issues footwork problems  and I feel like while there's a chance  he could be truly truly great there's a  greater chance that that it's just going  to be another one of these guys that a  few years from now we're talking about  him like we talked about Blaine Gabbert  Jake Locker Christian Ponder and all the  other guys that came in with a lot of  hype and promise and washed out without  doing much of anything  what should the Giants do it - I'd take  say Kwan Barkley I really would I would  not take a quarterback and I think when  Eli Manning comes out and says 37 isn't  old that's his code for don't take a  quarterback I intend to be here right so  I and and Tony Dungy made a great point  a few weeks ago he said that when he was  with the Steelers in the early eighties  they really liked Dan Marino but they  didn't want to have an awkward transfer  from Marino to Bradshaw Bradshaw to  Marino so they didn't do it so it comes  down to what do the Giants think of  these guys and I don't think there's a  guy that they feel strongly enough about  that that they'd be willing to deal with  the the back page of the tabloids and  the constant questions of when does Eli  Manning give way to the guy that they  took at number two instead you get  Barkley he makes your offense better  he makes Eli better Barkley Odell  Beckham jr. are you kidding me you don't  need an offensive line at all if you got  those two guys and I think that Barkley  makes the most sense for the Giants at -  do you make anything of Schad Khan  Jacksonville's owner buying Wembley  Stadium as to having a great home field  for an NFL team relocating there well  you know the knee-jerk reactions gonna  be that yeah hey the Jaguars are gonna  move to London and they're gonna say all  the right things that they're not gonna  leave Jacksonville but play this out at  some point that Stadium  in Jacksonville needs to be replaced and  when Schad Khan and the Jaguars start  asking for taxpayer money to build a new  stadium what if the politicians gonna  say I think I say you bought a stadium  in London why do you just buy some here  right so you quickly reach impasse over  the amount of taxpayer money that you  want and they can't get a deal done so  you move the team to London and sorry  it's not my fault the people in  Jacksonville didn't want to provide the  money  to build the stadium to keep the Jaguars  here and it won't surprise me if that's  the way it goes and if I'm an owner of  another team that's hoping to get  taxpayer money every time an owner buys  his own stadium I cringe because I know  I'm gonna have to deal with that now  when I try to shake free money out of  the trees because you've got Stan  Kroenke building that five billion  dollar complex and paying for it himself  in LA and you've got the Patriots that  own their stadium and now you've got a  guy who owns a stadium in another  country it just makes it harder and  harder to get taxpayer money and I'm not  saying it's right to get it I'm just  saying from a business standpoint these  owners like to be able to get it if they  can this is gonna make it even harder  thank you Mike have fun tonight we  appreciate your time all right Dan take  care Mike Florio Pro Football Talk  compro football talk on NBCSN for more  Dan Patrick show to the audience Channel  239 on DirecTV or download the Dan  Patrick show at  [Music]

